      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23 given that Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we need to calculate the number of days between these two dates and then determine the day of the week for December 23 based on that information.\n\n1. **Calculate the number of days between November 23 and December 23:**\n   - November has 30 days, so from November 23 to November 30 is \\(30 - 23 + 1 = 8\\) days.\n   - December has 31 days, so the number of days from December 1 to December 23 is 23 days.\n   - Therefore, the total number of days between November 23 and December 23 is \\(8 + 23 = 31\\) days.\n\n2. **Determine the day of the week for December 23:**\n   - Knowing that November 23 is a Thursday, we need to find out the day of the week for December 23. A week has 7 days, so we can find the equivalent day of the week by calculating the remainder when 31 is divided by 7.\n   - \\(31 \\div 7 = 4\\) remainder \\(3\\).\n   - A remainder of 3 means that 31 days is equivalent to 3 days after Thursday. Counting 3 days after Thursday, we get:\n     - Thursday + 1 day = Friday\n     - Friday + 1 day = Saturday\n     - Saturday + 1 day = Sunday\n   - Therefore, December 23 is a Sunday.\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\\).",
